26-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785936720281\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The scratch library is required by the agent library. Its purpose is to provide a safe hot-swappable scratchpad for the agent to build both transient code as well as 'skills' in the traditional agentic-harness sense. No production code lives there.\",\n    \"tags\": \"doctrine,scratch,skills,architecture\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner, in session, 2026-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785939038361\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The runtime library is not for code -- it is for local runtime values that don't belong in the botd.properties config files. It is gitignored (identity keys live there), so nothing in it rides canon.\",\n    \"tags\": \"doctrine,runtime,config,architecture\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner, in session, 2026-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785939038369\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Always fill out the desc field when writing a command, adding a control, or substantially altering a library. desc is discovery: MCP tools/list omits blank-desc commands entirely, and agents find controls through desc. upsert_command cannot set a desc, so creation must be followed by set_command_meta.\",\n    \"tags\": \"doctrine,desc,discovery,workflow,code\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner, in session, 2026-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785939038371\n  }\n]\n","old":"[\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Third party libraries should be avoided if at all possible. Mention tailwind again and you're dead to me.\",\n    \"tags\": \"doctrine,dependencies\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner, in session, 2026-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785934481082\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Threading is easy and cheap thanks to ndata.\",\n    \"tags\": \"doctrine,ndata,threading\",\n    \"source\": {\n 